ons cannot change.\nPlans persist. repeat counts complete executions, not rounds. Continuing work retains its exact operation, paid progress and reserved material; follow its cancellation contract. A global pause preserves costs. Normal satiety decline and successful outgoing messages do not stop plans. Urgent relevant messages, real failures, completed learning or new danger can cause a decision. Movement uses known geometry and real distance; an occupied coordinate is not a reachable meeting point. No effect happens merely because a plan describes it.\nReturn queries with result_json null, or queries=[] with result_json containing the JSON plan. A plan has intention:string, steps:[{action:{interface:string,args:object},repeat:positive integer,until:condition|null,guard:condition|null}], repeat:positive integer, until:condition|null, interrupts:string[], notes:string[], preferences:string[], projects:project[]. At most six steps, four projects and concise notes. A condition is {path,comparison,value}; comparison lt/lte/gt/gte/eq/neq; paths self.health/satiety/energy/temperature/happiness/inventory.RESOURCE or tick. Use interrupts=[] unless a supplied event is needed. A project has id,status(active/paused/completed/abandoned),question,evidence:string[],uncertainty,goal,completedSteps:string[],outputs:string[],missing,next,pauseReason,benefit. All other project fields are strings. Omitted projects persist. Give factual evidence and observed benefits, never claimed physical changes. Partial plans and protected-state edits are rejected.\nBatch up to four control queries. Each has section, search, ids:string[], offset>=0 and part>=0. Sections abilities/inventory/knowledge/projects/memory/state/observed; world may query only abilities. Exact IDs or text search; use empty search and ids for pagination. No implicit access outside this scope. Remaining query batches are explicit; when zero return a decision. Every model response, including retrieval and failure, consumes the shared budget.\nPlan horizon: every decision is a paid model response, while executing a plan is free. Prefer plans that cover the foreseeable routine for many rounds: give steps a repeat count with until (for example gather until an inventory amount, rest until energy is high), use plan repeat and until for cycles, and use guards and supplied interrupt events for conditions that should end the plan early. A single one-execution step is appropriate when its observed result decides what comes next.","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_00ac38cbc3311b6c016b054e444b5087d1b4e340bcacd09121","summary":[],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABrBU5EpjXV31gR1rouCYz1qOnxB5JYcUR-95sqYlkciBbbxCrSS8ZZhd4ir4C7NcG_ABN1xr4KSNIogw4GSsVG8k4fJYYkgfLmdCogW54HII2ZtmxL0nwI1ITXrJnA7nxu8ISEEaVMs2D7KvCDX_g57hktCby1Q_9t7QW9XnTo5t9kQJpA4FUuJ6SLm9KrWyp5AIxOmpqfJqv13CYWqCE7J7QtbjwcRidawMjqc5wiqmpM0uSRzRzAXhhE-Vwp3NSuSIzKojpvb7kFveRBih72tXPwhK52ftEVK3t1LgjMHcP3JFo9tA2bIQ6qlR5dA_FguKx71CGPPQWOw_7GSOuq_6B2cUTOB48jsKSGTeGB1RW7GhTROnKyCikUNvsI3efRe2GOXz4aD2OQpUBLfW-EBUlsyDG8TyrgO2EqMJUBljICD7v1RFguKyljXjXzDcIrc3QGSTv3KYeuR-sEbznxnyU5BwuWESweeeNqrXq_lTmQMiZJv4q0WP0VAWElYhr0_j044Uc81530VcPshbH-fRajwEssIzMYCRKR5LhKDyNeL7ONQTujW_1xrSUgQj8LmvOhy5itFFjrI4T5NXiep_Ox-c0gESL8D7g5j-6jwqEXqw2RsOYMAoRhlbdEcknpkARW2eYwzPLy5eB0a8ElyGj5IwekGr8nesROIFeCby7xnLKhxh7Q7LRsGrQ6A2r3ovCFaZmqoL4uhRCXWWhkdxYO2hqHS0etLFUTUsnXbrcL9oXDSt1E1yRNwE_EqUiwDY9twRUlmxo3R3kjH7gtBBNSjMcAjJHmVQsi48yFQUEoVIUctWMbSUbuEx0rks1T2qYtPLFzZbLP9G_im7Wgq_YD-gIvCwiFYa0ECWdZRxRaUcgrIxa51rULITpFo4TgOxP_swBNXN-XCN0bbvwKiNc0BAFcSyxay1JV4PflzRmh4vb9Jm8zWmn1PtJrTG3KFKkQEywfi73pjLWbbAE6p17LJyssXq65LiSlFmYtG37AuUF8O4DumBZcrGCAsp1dRH4gjwPvgt3zRtqfdmS8tk_KczNZ2NMp71S8RpyBfSfuJaVKT4DSxLRDfdm7csTKXTFIAGD__agOkB-T4Ssv8shqSwYPwkXmxbqWUxClm5HpX3KGYgQVDzhDlegrUpUJ1vXo1da6yFopPi0dJE7KWrj1NaBqpkvKk7YAvS3nG27usKF-mcGUymjI6O0j6qHh3_6d78eY_WJosfY871zNjJgdLwq4bbYLCBCV-i8o4s3Urw7FMGLDhtHX_qcSqj7Hefu8IqdxDtWHRrBlfoKQmDi19aIpNF-2ZGWnmvCp96E9wCZyiCnoa0FFPLk7WROHhqES